  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]≡¬(¬X∨¬Y)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬X∨¬Y)≡¬¬(X∧Y)\n$$\n\n- Finally,  we simplify the double negation:\n\n$$\n¬¬(X∧Y)≡X∧Y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡X∧Y\n$$",
